#!/opt/bin/perl

=head1 NAME

anyevent-mcp-askpermission - graphical or terminal permission helper

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<anyevent-mcp-askpermission> asks you whether an MCP tool may perform an
operation, such as reading a file or running a command. It shows the
requested operation and privileges, and lets you allow or deny it once,
or choose a rule for future requests.

Servers using L<AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Permissions> normally start this
helper automatically when a permission check needs your decision. The
helper displays a local graphical dialog or asks in a terminal, then
returns your choice to the server. You do not normally run it yourself.
To change saved rules later, use C<anyevent-mcp manage-rules NAME> or
C<anyevent-mcp edit-rules NAME>.

=head1 PERMISSION PROMPTS

The helper tries YAD first, leaving display backend selection to GTK.
If YAD cannot start, it asks on C</dev/tty>. Closing a working dialog,
terminal EOF, or having neither interface available means deny once.

Server, tool, action, workdir, subject and reason are shown as read-only
GTK labels when present, including the multibroker alias when available.
The requested sandbox grants appear together on one line. The initial YAD
form also has a C<Denial reason (optional)> field above four choices:
C<Deny once>, C<Deny always...>, C<Allow always...>, C<Allow once>.
The persistent rule editor can match the selected workdir (default) or any
configured workdir, including future ones. This changes rule matching,
not per-call sandbox grants.
One-time decisions are on the outside; C<Deny once>
uses YAD's default OK response. Closing the dialog also denies once.
The persistent choices open a separate rule editor for grant and scope
settings, including exact requested-file scope on deny rules. Rules can last
indefinitely (the default), 900 seconds or 16 hours. Expired rules disappear
when the rules are read and are removed from disk on the next ordinary save.
The reason
is included in a denial result but is ignored on an allowance.

Optional display-only request C<details> maps plain labels to Unicode text,
for example C<< { "View patch" => $diff } >>. Each entry appears as a size
summary and a button. YAD adds an ellipsis to the label and opens a separate,
read-only, resizable, monospace text window without dismissing the approval dialog.
Content is written to a private temporary UTF-8 file, never interpolated
into a command; control characters are escaped. The helper limits each
preview to 65536 Unicode characters and identifies incomplete previews.
Terminal and native MCP prompts include the same bounded text inline.
Display-only details never constrain or become part of persistent permission rules; an
C<allow-always> rule for C<perl -> permits future, different stdin scripts.

YAD uses GTK, so you can select a dark theme externally by setting
C<GTK_THEME=Adwaita:dark> in the server's environment before starting it.
The permission helper inherits that setting and passes it to YAD; the
theme is not changed for unrelated applications.

In a terminal, the four decisions are single-letter shortcuts and C<m>
edits the optional denial reason. Closing the dialog, cancelling or an unavailable
terminal denies once. Rule management remains separate:
C<anyevent-mcp manage-rules NAME> or C<anyevent-mcp edit-rules NAME>.


=head1 HELPER PROTOCOL

The helper reads one permission request on stdin and writes one JSON
decision on stdout. Servers invoke it through
L<AnyEvent::MCP::Permissions::Ask>, which describes the helper interface
and how to select a replacement helper. YAD's stderr is suppressed;
startup failure is detected from its exit status.

=head1 OPTIONS

=over

=item --manage-rules FILE

Open YAD rule list for FILE in evaluation order. Delete or reorder selected
rules. File lock protects updates; changes fail if list changed elsewhere.
Cannot combine with C<--edit-rules> or prompt-mode flags.

=item --edit-rules FILE

Edit permission rules in FILE using C<$VISUAL>, C<$EDITOR>,
C<sensible-editor> or C<vi>. Does not validate or overwrite editor output.
Cannot combine with C<--manage-rules> or prompt-mode flags.

=item --tty

Prompt only on C</dev/tty>, without YAD fallback. Unavailable terminal
denies access. Cannot combine with C<--yad> or rule-management flags.

=item --yad

Prompt only with YAD, without terminal fallback. Unavailable YAD
denies access. Cannot combine with C<--tty> or rule-management flags.

=item --help

Print short usage synopsis and exit.

=back

Without explicit C<--tty> or C<--yad>, prompts try YAD first, then
C</dev/tty> only if YAD cannot start. Closing or declining a working
dialog never triggers fallback.

=cut

use common::sense;

use Getopt::Long ();
use Text::ParseWords ();
use AnyEvent::MCP ();
use JSON::XS ();
use File::Temp ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Permissions::Ask ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Permissions ();

Getopt::Long::GetOptions (
   "manage-rules=s" => \my $rules_file, "edit-rules=s" => \my $edit_file,
   "tty" => \my $tty_only, "yad" => \my $yad_only, "help" => \my $help,
)
   or exit 2;
die "Unexpected arguments\n" if @ARGV || defined $rules_file && defined $edit_file;
die "--tty and --yad are mutually exclusive\n" if $tty_only && $yad_only;
die "--tty/--yad select permission prompts, not rule management\n"
   if ($tty_only || $yad_only) && (defined $rules_file || defined $edit_file);
if ($help) {
   print "usage: $0 [--tty | --yad | --manage-rules FILE | --edit-rules FILE]\n";
   exit;
}

binmode STDIN;
binmode STDOUT;

my $json = JSON::XS->new->canonical;
my $yad_pid;
$SIG{TERM} = $SIG{INT} = sub {
   if ($yad_pid) {
      kill TERM => $yad_pid;
      waitpid $yad_pid, 0;
   }
   exit 1;
};

sub yad {
   my $pid = open my $fh, "-|";
   return unless defined $pid;
   if (!$pid) {
      open STDERR, ">", "/dev/null" or exit 127;
      exec "yad", "--no-markup", map AnyEvent::MCP::utf8enc $_, @_;
      exit 127;
   }
   $yad_pid = $pid;
   local $/;
   my $output = <$fh>;
   close $fh;
   my $status = $?;
   undef $yad_pid;

   # our buttons never use 1: GTK display failure is not user cancellation.
   return if $status == 1 << 8 || $status == 127 << 8 || $status & 127;
   ($status >> 8, AnyEvent::MCP::utf8dec $output)
}

sub manage_rules {
   my ($file) = @_;

   my $permissions = AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Permissions->new;
   $permissions->{file} = $file;

   while (1) {
      my $rules = $permissions->rules;
      my ($status, $output) = yad (
         "--list", "--title=MCP permission rules", "--width=900", "--height=450",
         "--text=$file\nRules are evaluated from top to bottom; the first match wins.",
         "--column=Order:NUM", "--column=Decision", "--column=Action",
         "--column=Workdir", "--column=Subject", "--column=Sandbox grants", "--column=Expires",
         "--no-click", "--print-column=1", "--separator=\x1f",
         "--button=Close:0", "--button=Move up:4",
         "--button=Move down:6", "--button=Delete selected:2",
         map {
            my $rule = $rules->[$_];
            $_ + 1, $rule->{decision} || "ask",
            (map { exists $rule->{$_} ? $json->encode ($rule->{$_}) : "(any)" } qw(action workdir subject sandbox-grants)),
            (exists $rule->{expires} ? scalar localtime $rule->{expires} : "Indefinite")
         } 0 .. $#$rules,
      );
      die "YAD rule editor unavailable\n" unless defined $status;
      return unless grep $_ == $status, 2, 4, 6;
      my ($index) = $output =~ /\A([1-9][0-9]*)\x1f?\s*\z/;
      next unless $index && $index <= @$rules;
      next if $status == 4 && $index == 1;
      next if $status == 6 && $index == @$rules;
      my $expected = $json->encode ($rules);

      my $ok = eval {
         my $lock = $permissions->_lock;
         my $current = $permissions->rules;
         die "Permission rules changed since selection\n"
            unless $json->encode ($current) eq $expected;
         if ($status == 2) {
            splice @$current, $index - 1, 1;
         } else {
            my $other = $status == 4 ? $index - 2 : $index;
            @$current[$index - 1, $other] = @$current[$other, $index - 1];
         }

         # deletion does not need the application's capability implications.
         $permissions->{sandbox_grants} = {
            map { map { $_ => [] } split /,/, $_->{"sandbox-grants"} } @$current
         };
         $permissions->_write ($current);
         1
      };
      unless ($ok) {
         my $error = $@;
         print STDERR $error;
         yad "--title=MCP permission rules", "--text=$error", "--button=Close:0";
      }
   }
}

sub edit_rules {
   my ($file) = @_;

   my $permissions = AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Permissions->new;
   $permissions->{file} = $file;
   my $lock = $permissions->_lock; # Ensure the file exists and is private.
   close $lock or die "Cannot unlock permission rules: $!\n";

   for my $choice (grep { defined && /\S/ } @ENV{qw(VISUAL EDITOR)}, "sensible-editor", "vi") {
      my @editor = Text::ParseWords::shellwords ($choice);
      next unless @editor;

      my $status = system { $editor[0] } @editor, AnyEvent::MCP::utf8enc ($file);
      next if $status == -1;

      $status == 0
         or die "Editor failed or was interrupted (status $status)\n";

      return
   }

   die "No editor found (VISUAL, EDITOR, sensible-editor, vi)\n"
}
if (defined $rules_file) {
   eval { manage_rules AnyEvent::MCP::utf8dec $rules_file; 1 } or do {
      print STDERR $@;
      exit 1;
   };
   exit;
}

if (defined $edit_file) {
   eval { edit_rules AnyEvent::MCP::utf8dec $edit_file; 1 } or do {
      print STDERR $@;
      exit 1;
   };
   exit;
}

my $request = do { local $/; JSON::XS::decode_json (scalar <STDIN>) };
die "Invalid permission request\n" unless $request->{version} == 1;
my $subjects = $request->{subjects} || [];
my %decisions = (d => "deny-once", n => "deny-always", o => "allow-once", a => "allow-always");
my $persistent = !defined $request->{subject} || @$subjects;
my @deny_paths = grep defined && !ref, @{$request->{paths} || []};
my $unsandboxed = ($request->{sandbox_implementation} || "") =~ /\ANONE/;

sub rule_dialog {
   my ($choice, $message) = @_;

   my $allow = $choice eq "allow-always";
   my %selected = map { $_ => 1 } @{$request->{sandbox_grants}};
   my ($status, $output) = yad (
      "--form", "--title=Create MCP permission rule",
      "--width=650", "--separator=\x1f", "--item-separator=\x1f",
      "--num-output", "--always-print-result", "--buttons-layout=edge",
      "--text=Configure which future requests this rule covers."
         . (!$allow ? "\nDenial reason: " . (length $message ? $message : "(none)") : ""),
      "--button=Back:10", "--button=Save rule:8",
      ($allow ? (map {
         my $grant = $_;
         my $description = $request->{sandbox_grant_descriptions}{$grant};
         my $label = $grant . (defined $description && length $description ? " - $description" : "");
         $label =~ s/\\/\\\\/g;
         ("--field=$label:CHK", $selected{$grant} ? "TRUE" : "FALSE")
      } @{$request->{sandbox_grant_choices}}) : ()),
      (defined $request->{workdir} ? ("--field=Workdir scope:CB",
         "^1: This workdir\x1f2: Any configured workdir, including future ones") : ()),
      (@$subjects ? ("--field=Rule scope:CB", join "\x1f",
         map { ($_ == 0 ? "^" : "") . ($_ + 1) . ": " . $json->encode ($subjects->[$_]{label}) }
            0 .. $#$subjects) : ()),
      (!$allow && @deny_paths ? ("--field=Deny file scope:CB", join "\x1f",
         (map { ($_ == 0 ? "^" : "") . ($_ + 1) . ": Exact file " . $json->encode ($deny_paths[$_]) }
            0 .. $#deny_paths),
         scalar (@deny_paths + 1) . ": All paths") : ()),
      "--field=Rule lifetime:CB", "^Indefinite\x1f900 seconds\x1f16 hours",
   );
   return { decision => "back" } if $status == 10;
   return { decision => "deny-once" } unless $status == 8;
   my @values = split /\x1f/, $output, -1;
   my %answer = (decision => $choice, (!$allow && length $message ? (message => $message) : ()));
   if ($allow) {
      my @grants;
      for (@{$request->{sandbox_grant_choices}}) {
         my $value = shift @values;
         die "Invalid YAD sandbox grant selection\n" unless defined $value && $value =~ /\A(?:TRUE|FALSE)\z/i;
         push @grants, $_ if lc $value eq "true";
      }
      $answer{sandbox_grants} = \@grants;
   }
   if (defined $request->{workdir}) {
      my $index = shift @values;
      die "Invalid YAD workdir scope\n" unless defined $index && $index =~ /\A[12]\z/;
      $answer{workdir_scope} = "all" if $index == 2;
   }
   if (@$subjects) {
      my $index = shift @values;
      die "Invalid YAD rule scope\n" unless defined $index && $index =~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/
         && $index <= @$subjects;
      $answer{subject} = $subjects->[$index - 1]{subject};
   }
   if (!$allow && @deny_paths) {
      my $index = shift @values;
      die "Invalid YAD denial file scope\n" unless defined $index && $index =~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/
         && $index <= @deny_paths + 1;
      $answer{path} = $deny_paths[$index - 1] if $index <= @deny_paths;
   }
   my $lifetime = shift @values;
   defined $lifetime && $lifetime =~ /\A[123]\z/
      or die "Invalid YAD rule lifetime\n";
   $answer{lifetime} = ("indefinite", "900", "57600")[$lifetime - 1];

   \%answer
}

# display-only details are passed by filename, never through shell source text.
sub shell_quote {
   my $arg = shift;

   $arg =~ s/'/'\\''/g;
   "'$arg'"
}

sub display_text {
   my $text = shift;

   # render control and bidi characters explicitly, preserving tabs and newlines.
   $text =~ s/([\x00-\x08\x0b-\x1f\x7f-\x9f\x{202a}-\x{202e}\x{2066}-\x{2069}])/sprintf "\\u{%X}", ord $1/ge;
   $text
}

sub detail_fields {
   my @fields;

   for my $label (sort keys %{$request->{details} || {}}) {
      my $text = $request->{details}{$label};
      defined $text && !ref $text
         or die "Invalid permission detail\n";

      my $preview = AnyEvent::MCP::Permissions::Ask::detail_text $label, $text;
      my $chars = length $text;
      my $bytes = length AnyEvent::MCP::utf8enc $text;

      my ($fh, $filename) = File::Temp::tempfile (
         "mcp-permission-XXXXXXXX", TMPDIR => 1, UNLINK => 1);
      binmode $fh;
      print {$fh} AnyEvent::MCP::utf8enc ($preview)
         or die "Cannot write permission detail: $!\n";
      close $fh or die "Cannot close permission detail: $!\n";

      $label = display_text $label;
      $label =~ s/[:\t\n]/sprintf "\\u{%X}", ord $&/ge;
      my $info = "$label: $chars characters, $bytes UTF-8 bytes"
         . ($chars > 65536 ? " (incomplete preview)" : "");
      $info =~ s/\\/\\\\/g;
      my $button = $label;
      $button =~ s/\\/\\\\/g;

      push @fields,
         "--field=$info:LBL", "",
         "--field=$button...:FBTN",
         join " ", map shell_quote ($_),
            ("yad", "--no-markup", "--text-info",
             "--title=MCP permission: $label", "--width=900", "--height=650",
             "--fontname=Monospace 11", "--filename=$filename",
             "--button=Close:0");
   }

   @fields
}

sub graphical {
   if (($request->{_permission_stage} || "") eq "rule") {
      my $previous = $request->{_permission_selection};
      return rule_dialog ($previous->{decision}, $previous->{message} // "");
   }

   my @details = map {
      my $value = $request->{$_};
      $value = $_ eq "reason" ? display_text ($value)
         : ref $value || $value =~ /[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/ ? $json->encode ($value) : $value;
      $value =~ s/\\/\\\\/g;
      ({
         name                   => "Server",
         multibroker_alias      => "Multibroker alias",
         tool                   => "Tool",
         action                 => "Action",
         action_description     => "Action description",
         sandbox_implementation => "Sandbox",
         subject                => "Subject",
         workdir                => "Workdir",
         paths                  => "Paths",
         reason                 => "Reason",
      }->{$_} || ucfirst $_) . ": $value"
   } grep defined $request->{$_}, qw(name multibroker_alias tool action action_description sandbox_implementation workdir subject paths reason);

   my @view_fields = detail_fields;
   my $message = $request->{_permission_selection}{message} // "";
   while (1) {
      my ($status, $output) = yad (
         "--form", ($unsandboxed ? "--title=UNSANDBOXED MCP permission required"
                                  : "--title=MCP permission required"),
         "--width=650", "--height=400", "--scroll",
         "--text=" . ($unsandboxed
            ? "WARNING: NO SANDBOX. Workers run with all privileges of the host user.\n"
            : "")
            . "Required grants: " . join (" ", @{$request->{sandbox_grants}}),
         "--separator=\x1f", "--item-separator=\x1f", "--num-output", "--always-print-result",
         "--focus-field=" . (@details + @view_fields / 2 + 1),
         "--buttons-layout=edge",
         "--button=Deny once:0",
         ($persistent ? ("--button=Deny always...:6") : ()),
         ($persistent ? ("--button=Allow always...:8") : ()),
         "--button=Allow once:4",
         (map { ("--field=$_:LBL", "") } @details),
         @view_fields,
         "--field=Denial reason (optional)", $message,
      );
      return unless defined $status;
      return { decision => "deny-once" } unless grep $_ == $status, 0, 4, 6, 8;
      $message = (split /\x1f/, $output, -1)[@details + @view_fields / 2];
      die "Missing permission message field\n" unless defined $message;
      $message =~ s/\r?\n\z//;

      my $choice = {
         0 => "deny-once",
         4 => "allow-once",
         6 => "deny-always",
         8 => "allow-always",
      }->{$status};
      if ($choice =~ /-always\z/) {
         return { decision => $choice,
            ($choice eq "deny-always" && length $message ? (message => $message) : ()),
         } if ($request->{_permission_stage} || "") eq "choice";

         my $answer = rule_dialog ($choice, $message);
         next if $answer->{decision} eq "back";
         return $answer;
      }
      return {
         decision => $choice,
         ($status == 0 && length $message ? (message => $message) : ()),
         ($status == 4 ? (sandbox_grants => [@{$request->{sandbox_grants}}]) : ()),
      };
   }
}

sub terminal {
   open my $tty, "+<", "/dev/tty" or return { decision => "deny-once" };
   binmode $tty, ":encoding(UTF-8)";
   select ((select ($tty), $| = 1)[0]);

   my $ask = sub {
      print {$tty} $_[0] or die "Permission terminal: $!\n";
      my $answer = <$tty>;
      $answer =~ s/\s+\z// if defined $answer;
      $answer
   };

   my $message = $request->{_permission_selection}{message} // "";
   my $rule = sub {
      my ($choice) = @_;

      print {$tty} "Denial reason: ", (length $message ? $message : "(none)"), "\n"
         if $choice eq "deny-always";
      return { decision => "back" } if (($ask->("Configure future rule [Enter=continue, b=back]: ") // "b") eq "b");
      my %answer = (decision => $choice,
         ($choice eq "deny-always" && length $message ? (message => $message) : ()));
      if ($choice eq "allow-always") {
         print {$tty} "Available grants: ", join (", ", @{$request->{sandbox_grant_choices}}), "\n";
         my $caps = $ask->("Allowed grants [" . join (",", @{$request->{sandbox_grants}}) . "]: ");
         return { decision => "deny-once" } unless defined $caps;
         $answer{sandbox_grants} = [length $caps
            ? ($caps eq "-" ? () : split /\s*,\s*/, $caps, -1)
            : @{$request->{sandbox_grants}}];
      }
      if (defined $request->{workdir}) {
         print {$tty} "Workdir rule scope:\n",
            "1: This workdir\n",
            "2: Any configured workdir, including future ones\n";
         my $index = $ask->("Workdir scope [1]: ");
         return { decision => "deny-once" } unless defined $index;
         $index = 1 unless length $index;
         $index =~ /\A[12]\z/ or die "Invalid workdir scope\n";
         $answer{workdir_scope} = "all" if $index == 2;
      }
      if (@$subjects) {
         print {$tty} map { ($_ + 1) . ": " . $json->encode ($subjects->[$_]{label}) . "\n" }
            0 .. $#$subjects;
         my $index = $ask->("Persistent scope [1]: ");
         return { decision => "deny-once" } unless defined $index;
         $index = 1 unless length $index;
         die "Invalid persistent scope\n" unless $index =~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/ && $index <= @$subjects;
         $answer{subject} = $subjects->[$index - 1]{subject};
      }
      if ($choice eq "deny-always" && @deny_paths) {
         print {$tty} map { ($_ + 1) . ": " . $json->encode ($deny_paths[$_]) . "\n" }
            0 .. $#deny_paths;
         print {$tty} (@deny_paths + 1) . ": All paths\n";
         my $index = $ask->("Deny file scope [1]: ");
         return { decision => "deny-once" } unless defined $index;
         $index = 1 unless length $index;
         die "Invalid deny file scope\n" unless $index =~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/
            && $index <= @deny_paths + 1;
         $answer{path} = $deny_paths[$index - 1] if $index <= @deny_paths;
      }
      my $lifetime = $ask->("Rule lifetime [1=indefinite, 2=900 seconds, 3=16 hours; default 1]: ");
      return { decision => "deny-once" } unless defined $lifetime;
      $lifetime = 1 unless length $lifetime;
      $lifetime =~ /\A[123]\z/ or die "Invalid rule lifetime\n";
      $answer{lifetime} = ("indefinite", "900", "57600")[$lifetime - 1];

      \%answer
   };

   if (($request->{_permission_stage} || "") eq "rule") {
      return $rule->($request->{_permission_selection}{decision});
   }

   print {$tty} "\n\n******** MCP PERMISSION REQUIRED ********\n\n",
      AnyEvent::MCP::Permissions::Ask::message ($request),
      "\n\nThis is an approval prompt. No decision has been made.\n";

   while (1) {
      print {$tty} "\nDenial reason: ", (length $message ? $message : "(none)"), "\n",
         "  m  edit denial reason\n",
         "  o  allow once       d  deny once (default)\n",
         ($persistent ? "  a  allow always...  n  deny always...\n" : "");
      my $choice = $ask->("Choice [d]: ");
      return { decision => "deny-once" } unless defined $choice;
      $choice = "d" unless length $choice;

      if ($choice eq "m") {
         my $text = $ask->("Denial reason (Enter clears): ");
         return { decision => "deny-once" } unless defined $text;
         $message = $text;
         next;
      }

      next unless exists $decisions{$choice};
      next if !$persistent && $choice =~ /[na]/;
      my $decision = $decisions{$choice};
      if ($decision =~ /-always\z/) {
         return { decision => $decision,
            ($decision eq "deny-always" && length $message ? (message => $message) : ()),
         } if ($request->{_permission_stage} || "") eq "choice";

         my $answer = $rule->($decision);
         next if $answer->{decision} eq "back";
         return $answer;
      }
      return {
         decision => $decision,
         ($choice eq "d" && length $message ? (message => $message) : ()),
         ($choice eq "o" ? (sandbox_grants => [@{$request->{sandbox_grants}}]) : ()),
      };
   }
}

my $decision = eval {
   my $answer = $tty_only ? terminal : graphical;
   $answer = $yad_only ? { decision => "deny-once" } : terminal unless $answer;
   AnyEvent::MCP::Permissions::Ask::build ($request, $answer,
      $request->{_permission_stage}, $request->{_permission_selection})
};
if ($@) {
   print STDERR "Permission prompt failed; denied: $@";
   $decision = { decision => "deny-once" };
}
print JSON::XS::encode_json ($decision), "\n";
